msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:3
msgid "In most tools an unfinished thing is an error. In BDL it is a state. You can say _the lamp needs a brightness behavior_ before you know the formula, _there will be a temperature_ before you know how it is measured, _this output exists_ before anything drives it — and save, simulate what is ready, and check the rest tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/concepts/incomplete-designs.md:9
msgid "This page explains the states a design and its parts can be in, what each looks like, and which ones actually stop you."
