msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:47
msgid "**Diagnostics**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:47
msgid "`textDocument/diagnostic` (pull); `publishDiagnostics` only for clients without pull support"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:47
msgid "the same findings as Studio, with the same spans, in the file they belong to; _open_ findings come as information, not errors; findings about the source files (an unknown concept, a duplicate item, a second driver) are errors on the item"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:48
msgid "**Hover**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:48
msgid "`textDocument/hover`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:48
msgid "what a name is: a concept's value form and description, a relationship's signature and status, a component's ports, an instance's arguments and bound ports, a binding's ends"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:49
msgid "**Completion**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:49
msgid "`textDocument/completion`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:49
msgid "knows its scope: at an item start the items allowed there (a component body offers `requires`, `provides`, `use`, …); after `instance x :` the components; inside the braces the clock parameters and parameters not yet given; after `bind a.` the instance's ports; after `@` the domains in scope; in a body the body's own relationships and inputs, units after a number, `delay` / `sync` where allowed"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:50
msgid "**Go to definition**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:50
msgid "`textDocument/definition`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:50
msgid "by identity, across files — a concept from its use in a component, a component from its instance, a relationship from a call in a body"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:51
msgid "**References**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:51
msgid "`textDocument/references`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:51
msgid "every place the entity is named, in every file, including uses inside formula bodies"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:52
msgid "**Rename**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:52
msgid "`textDocument/prepareRename`, `textDocument/rename`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:52
msgid "renames the entity everywhere it is named, in every file, as text edits — concepts, relationships, components, ports, instances; parameter names are left alone"
