#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:55
msgid "**Document symbols**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:55
msgid "`textDocument/documentSymbol`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:55
msgid "the file's items"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:56
msgid "**Semantic tokens**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:56
msgid "`textDocument/semanticTokens/full`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:56
msgid "the standard token types your editor already themes — `type` for a concept, `function` for a rule, `variable` for a value (with the modifier `source` for a Source, `output`, `device`, `instance`), `namespace` for a clock, `class` for a component, `property` for a port, `parameter`, `keyword`, `number`, `operator`, `comment`, `enumMember` — plus BDL's own `unit` (the word after a number) and `slot` (the `?`); `declaration` on a declared name, `defaultLibrary` on an equation of the library; the same classes Studio colours"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:57
msgid "**Code actions**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:57
msgid "`textDocument/codeAction`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:57
msgid "the compiler's _fixes_ for findings in the range and context actions at the cursor. An action that changes only text carries its edit; one that would change the model or needs a choice is listed as **disabled** with the reason"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:58
msgid "**Cancellation**"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:58
msgid "`$/cancelRequest`"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:58
msgid "honoured; a cancelled request answers _RequestCancelled_"
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:60
msgid "Positions are negotiated in UTF-8, UTF-16 or UTF-32 as the client prefers; documents are synchronised in full on every change. Saving a file or changing one outside the editor (`workspace/didChangeWatchedFiles`) makes the server re-read the project."
msgstr ""

#: docs/user-guide/textual/editor-and-lsp.md:65
msgid "Custom requests for tools built on the server: `bdl/explainEntity` (the explanation of the entity at a position — the same content as Studio's _Explain_), `bdl/virtualDocument` (a read-only rendering: `explain` of the entity at a position or of the whole project, `core` — the design in kernel terms, `rust` — the generated core or why nothing is generated yet), `bdl/invalidationPreview` (what a model edit would reopen), and `bdl/previewEdit` (the full semantic plan of a rename). In VS Code these are the commands _BDL: Explain Entity at Cursor_, _BDL: Show Kernel Core_ and _BDL: Show Generated Rust_."
msgstr ""

